  "id": "038a3ce1-c76a-4e86-a458-2917d172e49d",
  "title": "Reasoning in Large Language Models: A Comparative Analysis",
  "summary": "This report investigates how large reasoning models (LRMs) perform on logical reasoning tasks compared to non-reasoning models. It highlights the challenges of aligning reasoning models with everyday logical reasoning and proposes new evaluation methods to improve their performance.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Large reasoning models (LRMs) achieve strong performance on mathematical and scientific benchmarks, but show degraded performance in everyday logical reasoning when reasoning deviates from formal logic.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Non-reasoning models with chain-of-thought prompting outperform comparable reasoning models in everyday reasoning tasks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prompting with additional instructions provides limited control over reasoning behavior, though it does not fully resolve the challenges of reasoning consistency.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Competence-based evaluation (CBE) is proposed as a new paradigm to measure a model's generalization capacity in reasoning, focusing on reliable application of a competence across a family of problems.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "geography": "Global",
